Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q1 (gzip SSE is the normal case), Q2 (event, delta and block names), Q7 (decode cap makes a cut partial)
Why this approach: a line reader over the decoded copy dispatches events at blank lines and drops a trailing event with no end, so a cut body never reads as malformed data. Each block index has a builder; a block no delta touched is kept byte for byte, otherwise its start object gets text and thinking joined, signature set, citations appended and input set to the joined JSON, read only at content_block_stop. The JSON and SSE paths share assistantEvents, so a streamed response canonicalizes to exactly the JSON response's events (TestParse_NonStreaming compares them). Usage keys from message_start and every message_delta are merged, last non-null value wins. Details recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T22").
Alternatives rejected: parsing each partial_json prefix as it arrives (the spec reads it only at the stop); rebuilding every block through a map even with no deltas (loses the sent bytes of unknown and redacted_thinking blocks); a separate raw-string field on core.Block for a bad tool input (core change for one adapter; the tool event's input carries the raw joined string as a JSON string instead).
Trade-off / known limit: a stream that ends in an error event after message_start is partial (the message never reached message_stop); an error-only stream is ok. The in-stream error event carries the HTTP status (200). A non-2xx response with an event-stream content type is read as JSON, so it is failed with a status-only error event. message_start's id and model have no canonical field and stay in the raw body only. A delta or stop for a block that never started makes the parse partial.
Verified by: make verify (go test -race ./...). Tests first failed for the right reason: GoldenStream, UnknownBlockAndEventKept, ToolInputSplitAcrossDeltas, ThinkingSignatureKept, RedactedThinkingKept/streamed, UsageLastValueWins, TruncatedStreamPartial, TruncatedToolInputPartial, UpstreamError/sse_error_event, NonStreaming (streamed equivalent) all found no response events; GoldenStreamGzip and ContentEncodings passed on arrival (both sides empty) and gained a guard that the identity stream gives 4 events. Also added: TestParse_StreamWithoutStopPartial, TestParse_MalformedStreamFailed, TestParse_StreamLineEnds. Mutation, reverted: parsing a tool input without its stop failed TruncatedToolInputPartial/valid_prefix_no_stop. TestFixtures_NoIdentifiers passes over the new fixture and golden.
